    {
      "id": "WeA_D2k5_8D6d5aBPl4xH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2439.913452936673,
      "y": -1884.9978051195767,
      "width": 847.2898404950887,
      "height": 158.86684509282907,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b04",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 616439200,
      "version": 137,
      "versionNonce": 526513568,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792925276058,
      "created": 1792925258620,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "<!doctype html>: The doctype is a required preamble. In the mists of time, when HTML\nwas young (around 1991/92), doctypes were meant to act as links to a set of rules that\nthe HTML page had to follow to be considered good HTML, which could mean\nautomatic error checking and other useful things. However, these days, they don't do\nmuch and are basically just needed to make sure your document behaves correctly.\nThat's all you need to know for now.",
      "fontSize": 21.182246012377227,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "<!doctype html>: The doctype is a required preamble. In the mists of time, when HTML was young (around 1991/92), doctypes were meant to act as links to a set of rules that the HTML page had to follow to be considered good HTML, which could mean automatic error checking and other useful things. However, these days, they don't do much and are basically just needed to make sure your document behaves correctly. That's all you need to know for now.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "TLvlNe1d3w0lUV0WDjo4K",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2442.272007379801,
      "y": -1707.302463540808,
      "width": 887.797629301585,
      "height": 111.15827697075083,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b05",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 633347168,
      "version": 54,
      "versionNonce": 1992788064,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792925309960,
      "created": 1792925303705,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "<meta charset=\"utf-8\">: This element sets the character set your document should use\nto UTF-8, which includes most characters from the vast majority of written languages.\nEssentially, it can now handle any textual content you might put on it. There is no reason\nnot to set this, and it can help avoid some problems later on.",
      "fontSize": 22.23165539415017,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "<meta charset=\"utf-8\">: This element sets the character set your document should use to UTF-8, which includes most characters from the vast majority of written languages. Essentially, it can now handle any textual content you might put on it. There is no reason not to set this, and it can help avoid some problems later on.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "eV6J0tR3pR507JkJwQ8gh",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2440.6697898010975,
      "y": -1578.4375751315479,
      "width": 893.3580615552748,
      "height": 84.56423740350078,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b06",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1242099808,
      "version": 93,
      "versionNonce": 1608282208,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792925336479,
      "created": 1792925323817,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width\">: This viewport element\nensures the page renders at the width of the browser viewport, preventing mobile\nbrowsers from rendering pages wider than the viewport and then shrinking them down.",
      "fontSize": 22.550463307600207,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width\">: This viewport element ensures the page renders at the width of the browser viewport, preventing mobile browsers from rendering pages wider than the viewport and then shrinking them down.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "LL6TsAo8LIpql-vgRL2Fg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2444.6955716384236,
      "y": -1470.5475176345408,
      "width": 913.3539247822314,
      "height": 256.8807913450027,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b07",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 972007840,
      "version": 112,
      "versionNonce": 1423376800,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792925381223,
      "created": 1792925366635,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "We have also included an alt (alternative) attribute. In the alt attribute, you specify\ndescriptive text for users who cannot see the image, possibly because of the following\nreasons:\n\nThey are visually impaired. Users with significant visual impairments often use tools\ncalled screen readers to read out the alt text to them.\n\nSomething has gone wrong, causing the image not to display. If the src attribute does\nnot contain a valid path to an image, the alt text will be displayed instead:",
      "fontSize": 22.8338481195558,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "We have also included an alt (alternative) attribute. In the alt attribute, you specify descriptive text for users who cannot see the image, possibly because of the following reasons:\n\nThey are visually impaired. Users with significant visual impairments often use tools called screen readers to read out the alt text to them.\n\nSomething has gone wrong, causing the image not to display. If the src attribute does not contain a valid path to an image, the alt text will be displayed instead:",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "xp49sMH998CU5J0915DCE",
      "type": "text",
